    "notes": [
      "Scope is the BeSpoke direct editor only. direct-editor.css overrides the inherited builder and guide chrome; builder-model.mjs supplies cumulative slide and thumbnail styles.",
      "Tonal ramps are synthesized OKLCH display aids for the documentation panel, not new runtime palette tokens or extra selectable colors.",
      "Component snippets are static visual examples. Application event handlers, tab keyboard behavior, draft logic, and role-contrast validation remain in builder-app.mjs and builder-model.mjs.",
      "No authored transition or animation token exists in the current chrome. Reduced-motion preferences disable animation, transitions, and smooth scrolling.",
      "Mobile uses a horizontal thumbnail strip and contextual toolbar, with the canvas always visible. The inherited Design / Preview switch is hidden.",
      "Direct selection and inspector state remain transient UI state. Role typography uses existing roleStyles; optional saved boxStyles holds four fill/border/look records.",
      "Compact chrome typography is descriptive evidence, not blanket authorization for smaller reading text or proof of accessibility."
    ]
